[agent] - **f1**: Q25/Q50/Q75 = -0.597 / 0.124 / 0.834, mean 0.123, std 1.02 — clean ~N(0,1)
[agent] - **f2**: -0.686 / 0.102 / 0.846, mean 0.087, std 1.07 — clean ~N(0,1)
[agent] - **f3**: -0.570 / 0.141 / 0.799, mean 0.122, std 0.97 — clean ~N(0,1)
[agent] - **f4**: -0.659 / 0.051 / 0.720, mean 0.027, std 1.00 — clean ~N(0,1)
[agent] - **f5**: -0.707 / 0.013 / 0.625, mean 0.000, std 0.98 — clean ~N(0,1)
[agent] - **f6**: Q25 = -0.055, Q50 = 0.110, **Q75 = 2.399**, min -0.406, max 2.843, mean 0.839 — **sharply bimodal**
[agent] f6 is the only feature that is bimodal: a low cluster near 0 and a high cluster near ~2.4. The mass split lands exactly between Q50 and Q75 — i.e. ~66% of rows are in the low cluster and ~34% in the high cluster, which matches the positive-label rate exactly (label mean = 0.339 → 33.9% positives). That's the signature of a feature deterministically derived from the outcome (≈0 when label=0, ≈2.4 when label=1, plus small noise), confirmed by the raw rows (f6≈2.3–2.5 ⇔ label=1).
